  "notes": "Source: Agape College of Business and Science 2023 Catalog (Revision and Print Date 03/25/2024), official PDF at acbscollege.org. Hand-transcribed 2026-09-30. QUARTER CREDITS: Agape uses a quarter-based calendar; all credit values in this file are QUARTER credits as stated in the catalog (p. 'Academic credit is given in quarter credits'). They are not semester credits. Catalog degree outlines give lecture/lab/externship hours per course; only the catalog's stated quarter-credit values are transcribed here. Quarter-by-quarter term placement is the collector's arrangement (the catalog lists courses in tables, not term sequences) and follows catalog prerequisite chains; this is disclosed, not a catalog claim. Prerequisites transcribed only from the catalog's course-description sections (asterisk legend rules applied per program); non-course prerequisites (e.g., 'all courses prior to the last quarter of enrollment') are recorded in choice_note instead of prereq. Program totals: concentration + elective 120, general education 60 = 180 quarter credits (catalog: 2160 total hours). As in the BSBA plan, the catalog's 'Elective Total 13' is a categorization within the listed concentration courses (listed courses sum to 120); no separate electives are named. Catalog asterisk rules applied: '*BUS112' prereq on ACC213/MED-area courses is 'Not applicable for the BS in HCA'; '*BUS114' on BUS216 likewise; ECN214 prereq '*BUS112 ... Not applicable for the BS in HCA' -> no prereq; '*BUS112' on MTH306 and SOC325 is 'Not applicable for the BS in HCA' -> MTH306 prereq [MTH106], SOC325 [ENG104, MTH106]. HCA318 prereqs per catalog: HCA201, HCA316. MED207 is 4 quarter credits per the program outline (the BS HCA course-description page says 3; the outline and degree total use 4). Exit requirements (not modeled): 150 externship hours (MED209), 90 internship hours (HCA332), capstone project, 70% overall GPA. Note: the program description paragraph says '107 credit of core courses,' which conflicts with the outline table (concentration + elective 120, general education 60 = 180); this plan follows the outline table and its stated 180-unit total.",
